      "problem": {
        "original_text": "Let (X,Y) have joint density f(x,y) = 2 on the triangle 0 < y < x < 1, and 0 otherwise. Verify that f is a valid joint density by integrating over its support. Compute the marginal density f_X(x). Compute the marginal density f_Y(y). Compute E[X] and E[Y]. Compute P(Y < 1/4). Compute the conditional density f_{Y|X}(y|x). Compute E[Y|X=x] and simplify. Compute Cov(X,Y). Find the correlation Corr(X,Y) and interpret its sign.",
